{
  "case_id": "2006-05-915",
  "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We'll hear argument next in 05-915, Meredith versus Jefferson County Board of Education."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Teddy B. Gordon",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Crystal Meredith wanted to do what most moms and dads do all across this country. She wanted to put her son's hand in hers and walk around the corner and enroll her son in school."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But she, she could have -- if she had been there at the deadline, the child would have been admitted to -- if she had been there in March instead of August?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Justice Souter, this Court over and over again has said once a remedial plan is accepted there should be race-neutral alternatives under the narrow and tailored requirement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And isn't there a distinction between unitary status and unitary condition? Unitary condition is a descriptive situation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0000-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner's son was denied the opportunity to transfer from Young Elementary School to Bloom Elementary School solely on the basis of his race."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question is: Why do thy have to hide the ball by saying, oh, we're going to consider these other things, ability to teach, educational credits, whatever you could come up with when at the beginning and at the end, the objective is to achieve a racial mix? Why can't they do that candidly and employ a criterion that candidly addresses that objective?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Francis J. Mellen, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MELLEN: I think, Your Honor, that Brown is very much distinguishable. In Brown, the Topeka board maintained two systems of schools. And admission to those schools, admission, not assignment, was based solely on race. That stigmatized the black children. It sent the message that the white race was dominant and superior and that the black race was inferior. That caused great harm to those black students and this Court properly remediated it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are there circumstances under which there is reason to suspect the motivation of school districts when they come up with a plan in effect to require a mixing of the races in the schools that is more or less tailored to the relative percentages in the communities? Is -- are there circumstances in which that would be done for malign as opposed to benign purposes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why did you say -- in truth, maybe I missed it. In your response to Justice Kennedy, I think you said, when he asked, that this Court has never said that the explicit use of race by a K through 12 school board was constitutional, and I thought the Court had explicitly said that in Swann."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. MELLEN",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do not contend, Your Honor, that the purpose of this plan is to remediate past discrimination against black students. This plan is intended to provide benefits to both black and white students."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it were to become relevant, would this record show -- this is the school district -- and this would be in the regime of the Court-ordered desegregation plan, because you are just recently emerged from that -- that the school district has tried means other than race conscious, of race classification in order to obtain the diversity benefits you seek?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But your starting place was the plan that was compulsory, that was forced on the school district in 1975? That is basically the same kind of plan?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. MELLEN",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7eb1b6388d3a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All of those scenarios show substantial resegregation, particularly in elementary schools."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-915",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "7eb1b6388d3a1c74f9a46437c32eaf3cc6d6029b5aed50bf433106001b7834b2",
